Embedded Windowed Multipole data (MIT CRPG — NOT NJOY / NOT LANL)
----------------------------------------------------------------

This crate ALSO embeds a windowed-multipole cross-section data set
(`src/data/wmp_core.wmpl`, the CORE 125-nuclide blob decoded by
`wmp::WmpLibrary` / `wmp::WindowedMultipole`). That data is a SEPARATE work
from NJOY2016:

- Source:  MIT Computational Reactor Physics Group (CRPG) `WMP_Library`,
  https://github.com/mit-crpg/WMP_Library (ENDF/B-VII.1 evaluations).
- Copyright:  © 2018-2021 Massachusetts Institute of Technology.
- License:  MIT (full text in `LICENSE-WMP`). MIT is GPL-compatible, so it
  coexists with this crate's overall `GPL-3.0-only` licensing.
- The windowing/curve-fit method is that of C. Josey, P. Romano, B. Forget,
  and K. Smith (MIT CRPG). This attribution is DISTINCT from the NJOY/LANL
  attribution above; do not conflate the two, and do not imply LANL endorsement
  of the WMP data.

The `wmp` module's evaluation algorithm is an independent Rust re-implementation
(reference: OpenMC's MIT-licensed `src/wmp.cpp`); only the numeric data blob is
derived from `WMP_Library`.
